# Copy this file to `.env` (same folder) and fill in what you need.
# `.env` is ignored by Git: your keys never reach the public repository.
# Every variable is optional; the app works without any key (degraded mode, no AI).

# --- Server (loopback only: any other host is refused at startup) ---
VOCAB_HOST=127.0.0.1
VOCAB_PORT=8000

# --- Where personal data lives (database, audio). Default: ./data ---
# VOCAB_DATA_DIR=C:\Users\me\vocab-coach-data
# A relative VOCAB_DATA_DIR is taken from the repository root, never from the current folder.

# --- Database (SQLite). Default: <VOCAB_DATA_DIR>/vocab-coach.sqlite3 ---
# Only set this to use another file. Use forward slashes, even on Windows:
# VOCAB_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///C:/Users/me/vocab-coach-data/other.sqlite3
# Created and upgraded by start.cmd / start.ps1 / start.sh, or by hand:
#   cd backend; uv run python -m app db upgrade

# --- AI providers (free tiers; leave empty or commented out for "not configured") ---
# The app works without any key: usage sheets, corrections and speech transcription are then
# unavailable, everything else (reviews, error log, statistics) keeps working.
# Gemini API key (main text provider; create it in Google AI Studio):
# VOCAB_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Groq API key (text fallback and Whisper transcription; create it in the Groq console):
# VOCAB_GROQ_API_KEY=
# With this key, your speaking recordings are sent to Groq's free tier to be transcribed: they
# leave this computer. They are stored in <VOCAB_DATA_DIR>/audio/ (audio-demo/ for the demo
# data), never in Git. Without a key they stay local and are not transcribed.
# Base URL of a local Ollama server (optional, offline use). Write it as 127.0.0.1: on Windows,
# `localhost` may resolve to the IPv6 address ::1 first, where Ollama does not listen. 11434 is
# Ollama's default port:
# VOCAB_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# The order in which providers are tried is the `ai_provider_order` setting (default: gemini, groq,
# ollama), not an environment variable. Keys are only ever read by the backend.
#
# Model names (optional). Leave empty to use the defaults built into the app; `python -m app ai
# status` shows the models in use. Set one only if a provider retires its default model.
# VOCAB_GEMINI_MODEL=
# VOCAB_GROQ_TEXT_MODEL=
# VOCAB_GROQ_TRANSCRIPTION_MODEL=
# VOCAB_OLLAMA_MODEL=
#
# Check your setup (one real request per provider; it uses a little of the free quota):
#   cd backend; uv run python -m app ai status
#   cd backend; uv run python -m app ai test

# --- Pronunciation assessment (milestone M6, optional, disabled by default) ---
# VOCAB_AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
# VOCAB_AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=
